3:["$","p","These materials pair beautifully with Fl",{"children":"These materials pair beautifully with Florida's coastal and tropical design aesthetics. The natural imperfections in woven materials create visual interest that mass-produced alternatives can't replicate."}]
4:["$","p","For practicality, look for woven options",{"children":"For practicality, look for woven options with UV-protective liner backing. This preserves the natural look from the room side while adding the sun protection and privacy that raw natural materials alone can't provide."}]
5:["$","div","2",{"className":"flex flex-col items-start","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-[18px] font-semibold leading-[27px] tracking-[-0.0648px] text-navy","children":"3. Layered Treatment Combinations"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-4 flex flex-col gap-[23px] text-[16px] leading-[23px] text-navy","children":[["$","p","The trend toward layering multiple windo",{"children":"The trend toward layering multiple window treatments offers both design flexibility and functional versatility. A common combination pairs sheer curtain panels with cellular shades behind them."}],["$","p","Layering allows you to shift between dif",{"children":"Layering allows you to shift between different levels of light, privacy, and insulation throughout the day without changing any single treatment. Sheers soften harsh sunlight; the shade behind provides full blackout when needed."}],["$","p","Color coordination across layers creates",{"children":"Color coordination across layers creates depth and sophistication. A monochromatic approach (varying shades of the same color) reads as elegant, while contrasting layers make a bolder design statement."}]]}]]}]
6:["$","div","3",{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 md:grid-cols-3","children":[["$","div","Minimalist motorized roller shade in a modern office",{"className":"relative h-[240px] overflow-hidden rounded-lg md:h-[280px] xl:h-[359px]","children":["$","$L2",null,{"src":"/images/resources/knowledge-grid-1.webp","alt":"Minimalist motorized roller shade in a modern office","fill":true,"className":"object-cover"}]}],["$","div","Woven bamboo shades in a coastal living room",{"className":"relative h-[240px] overflow-hidden rounded-lg md:h-[280px] xl:h-[359px]","children":["$","$L2",null,{"src":"/images/resources/knowledge-grid-2.webp","alt":"Woven bamboo shades in a coastal living room","fill":true,"className":"object-cover"}]}],["$","div","Layered sheer curtains with cellular shades behind",{"className":"relative h-[240px] overflow-hidden rounded-lg md:h-[280px] xl:h-[359px]","children":["$","$L2",null,{"src":"/images/resources/knowledge-grid-3.webp","alt":"Layered sheer curtains with cellular shades behind","fill":true,"className":"object-cover"}]}]]}]
7:["$","div","4",{"className":"flex flex-col items-start","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-[18px] font-semibold leading-[27px] tracking-[-0.0648px] text-navy","children":"4. Bold Color and Pattern Revival"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-4 flex flex-col gap-[23px] text-[16px] leading-[23px] text-navy","children":[["$","p","After years of neutral dominance, bold c",{"children":"After years of neutral dominance, bold colors and patterns are returning to window treatments. Deep jewel tones — emerald, sapphire, and burgundy — add drama and sophistication to rooms that previously played it safe."}],["$","p","Geometric patterns and botanical prints ",{"children":"Geometric patterns and botanical prints on roller shades and roman shades bring personality without requiring a full room redesign. These statement treatments work best when the rest of the room maintains a neutral palette."}],["$","p","For those not ready to commit fully, col",{"children":"For those not ready to commit fully, colored trim, banding, and borders on otherwise neutral treatments offer a measured way to incorporate the trend while keeping the flexibility to update the look seasonally."}]]}]]}]
